On Wed, 31 Dec 2008, Matt Frisch wrote:
> Just curious, but why leather over dexterity...ever? Obviously if the
> leather are fireproof +5s vs +0 dex that's a no-brainer, but they're the
> same weight, same armor, same...protection-provided-by-gloves for footrices
> and the like, why not dex?

There is actually a major practical situation where leather beats
dexterity.  You cannot exercise a stat if its *effective* value is 18 or
higher.  So if you acquired +5 [GoD early and wore them, your base
dexterity would stall at 13.

It's then wiser to wear leather until your dexterity reaches 18 naturally
-- then the gloves will let you reach a dexterity of 23.

That said, dexterity isn't really that important.  [GoD seems to be a
"DevTeam trap" that lures [GoP-hating players into leaving their [LG at
non-burnproof +0 so as to save their ?oEA for the [GoD they hope to
eventually find.  But I'm a sucker for it....

